90437903","ID":"NO_40CCX0gOkWuOsQu","UserID":"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg","Timestamp":1661331722,"Removed":false},{"Message":"https:\/\/www.researchgate.net\/publication\/247515539_The_Effects_of_a_Mental_Training_Program_on_Juniors_Pre-Competitive_Anxiety_Self-Confidence_and_Tennis_Performance","ID":"NO_dbQRBQ8WEZSoXGu","UserID":"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg","Timestamp":1661331728,"Removed":false},{"Message":"e. Specifically, each player was asked to appraise his or her performance on\na 5-point scale (1 being \u201cnot good at all\u201d and 5 being \u201cvery good\u201d) on the following aspects:\n1) his or her physical feelings; 2) quality of technique; 3) timing and rhythm; 4) concentration;\n5) amount of effort exerted; 6) mental attitude and thoughts; 7) level of self-confidence during\nthe match; and 8) comparison of his or her performance with what he or she was expected to\nplay, given the opponent. An overall performance score was obtained from the sum of all these\n8 items","ID":"NO_2shasxveY1g1wbQ","UserID":"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg","Timestamp":1661331758,"Removed":false}],"UserStatuses":{"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg":"Expanded"},"ParentID":"QID84","ID":"NT_a5lx0ICf7HgLnee"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_9HbTfKIyuQpMsku","Element":"NT","PrimaryAttribute":"NT_bIxpp6jWKu2G32u","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"Notes":[{"Message":"https:\/\/veronikahuta.weebly.com\/","ID":"NO_e5rqMvfZS7knBgq","UserID":"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg","Timestamp":1661330901,"Removed":false},{"Message":"Huta, V., & Ryan, R. M. (2010). Pursuing pleasure or virtue: The differential and overlapping well-being benefits of hedonic and eudaimonic motives. Journal of Happiness Studies, 11, 735-762","ID":"NO_6m1AVJjpr7H0kse","UserID":"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg","Timestamp":1661330925,"Removed":false},{"Message":"hedonic items: 1,4,6,7,9\neudaimonic items: 2,3,5,8","ID":"NO_bKS9LzoXsZxNKtg","UserID":"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg","Timestamp":1662040466,"Removed":false}],"UserStatuses":{"UR_3klMX9YtgrEA7Hg":"Expanded"},"ParentID